From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baptiste Augrain <daiyam@zokugun.org>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: split vscode build into a shared prepack task and per-target packing
 tasks

Compiling core and the built-in extensions is platform- and arch-independent, so it is factored into a standalone `prepack` task keyed only by minification while the platform/arch-specific bundling becomes a separate `packing` task; both are registered as top-level gulp tasks so the compile stage can run once and be reused across every packaging target instead of being repeated per target.

`semver` is also kept out of `node_modules.asar`: the update service imports it statically into the main ESM bundle, and node resolves a module's static imports before that bundle's body runs and registers the archive's loader hook, so it has to exist as a real file.

